1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:07,780
A stop loss limits your loss. A take profit locks in your gain.

2
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:11,600
Right click your trade and choose Stop.

3
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,960
Set the price where you want to get out if the market goes against you.

4
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:20,460
It shows the distance in points and what you would lose.

5
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:26,070
Click OK.

6
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:34,040
The stop loss now shows in the Stop column.

7
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:37,850
For a take profit, right click the trade and choose Limit.

8
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:42,210
Set the price where you want to take your profit.

9
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:46,190
Again it shows the distance and what you would make.

10
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:51,810
Click OK.

11
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:55,810
Now the trade has both: a stop loss and a take profit.

